# Child worlds report

30 child research worlds were made with `researchworld run` (topic "Child N: ...", the supplied child-config.json). `world_status` is taken from `researchworld status <world>` at report time (for Child 1 the top-level field; for the others, which carry no top-level field, `bootstrap.world_status`, shown with the scheduler status).

- **Driven** (`execute <world> --loop`, all three ended): Child 1 `rw_8cb26d5357f8`, Child 2 `rw_bb2bb710fde3`, Child 3 `rw_729502c68fc1`.
- **Finished** (`researchworld finish`, after all three drives ended): Child 1 `rw_8cb26d5357f8` only.
- The other 27 were left untouched.
- Disclosure: `run` prints its JSON to stderr; ids were lost in a first batch and I re-ran Child 2 once, creating an extra duplicate world `rw_d427cac4346b`. It is not one of the 30, was not driven or finished, and is listed last.

